        <briefdescription>
<para>Equality comparison operator to compare an ID value with the invalid ID constant. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This operator allows for direct comparison between an ID value and the <computeroutput>invalid_id</computeroutput> constant, enabling easy checking if a given ID is invalid without needing to explicitly reference the <computeroutput>invalid_id_v</computeroutput> constant for the specific ID type.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>IdType</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the ID, which must satisfy the <ulink url="gl_concepts.md#gl-traits-c-id-type"><bold>c_id_type</bold></ulink> concept. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>lhs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The ID value to compare againsyt the invalid ID constant. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>rhs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The <computeroutput>invalid_id</computeroutput> constant (of type <computeroutput><ref refid="structgl_1_1invalid__id__t" kindref="compound">invalid_id_t</ref></computeroutput>) to compare with the ID value. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Returns <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if <computeroutput>lhs</computeroutput> is equal to the invalid ID value for its type, and <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> otherwise. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
